    {
      "name": "nivo_stop_answer",
      "title": "Answer a run's open stop as stop",
      "description": "Answer a run's open stop as stop.list shows it: the founder's words (answer, with text), retry the step, take the conversation over, or skip (ends the run, keeping what was done). An approval stop takes its verdict through run.step.decide instead. Owner or manager. The answer is recorded and handed to the agent's engine, which resumes the run's thread shortly after: read run.get or stop.list again for its next state. Answers the outcome (admitted, already_admitted, already_answered, stop_closed, step_running, not_stopped, approval_pending with the door that takes the verdict, ...) and the step. (NIVO op nivo.api.nivo.stop.answer; needs an opKey; destructive: ask your user first.)",
